To work out the types (list of text) of a species (text):
  Let the entry be the species types for the species.
  If the entry is nothing:
    Fail because "No types for {the species}.".
  If the entry's second type is "":
    The answer is a list of the entry's first type.
  The answer is a list of the entry's first type and the entry's second type.

To work out the type factor (number) of an attacking type (text) against a defending type (text):
  Let the matchup be the type matchups for "{the attacking type} {the defending type}".
  The answer is the matchup's multiplier or else 1.

To work out the effectiveness (number) of an attacking type (text) against a species (text):
  Let the result be 1.
  For each defending type in the types of the species:
    Set the result to the result * (the type factor of the attacking type against the defending type).
  The answer is the result.
